      "transcript": {},
      "analysis": {
        "path": "analysis/PjObX9XQvgI.analysis.json",
        "schema_version": 2,
        "model": "gpt-5-nano"
      },
      "summary": "Justin Brown (Primal Video) demonstrates eight AI-powered features now available in Adobe Premiere Pro, highlighting how these tools speed editing and enable new workflows. The guide covers audio remix to extend or shorten music with automated seam blending, generative extend to lengthen video clips (up to a two-second AI-generated extension) and identify AI-generated portions, AI text-based editing through transcription (including language detection, speaker labeling, and editing from text), automatic captions export, enhanced speech for noisy audio, scene edit detection to insert cuts at shot changes, morph cut to smooth over jump cuts, AI reframing for auto-scene repositioning when changing aspect ratios, auto reframe sequencing for multi-clip projects, and AI-assisted color correction via Lumetri Auto with adjustable intensity. Throughout, the presenter notes practical caveats (e.g., 2-second extension limit, occasional perceptual differences in color correction, and verification of AI-generated edits). The video provides concrete steps and UI cues (e.g., locating Remix in the rate-stretch menu, selecting AI-generated regions, using Transcribe and the Lumetri Color tab) to help learners apply these features in real-world projects.",
